From 552cfa556b9e99aad66a207cbf098778e2a67bb5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 17:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] patches/openwrt: fix WS-AP3715i bootwrapper link address

The Enterasys WS-AP3715i cannot boot any 24.10-based image: the board
hangs with no output at all right after U-Boot prints "Uncompressing
Kernel Image ... OK".

p1010.mk pins KERNEL_LOADADDR to 0x1500000, but the simpleImage
bootwrapper picks its own link address and ws-ap3715i was never added to
the case in arch/powerpc/boot/wrapper that pins it to the same value.
It therefore gets the 0x400000 default plus make_space=y, which rounds
the link address up to the next MiB above the uncompressed kernel - so
the link address follows the kernel size while the uImage header does
not, and the position-dependent wrapper is entered at the wrong address.

This is what made it look like a squashfs-only bug: on 24.10 the
initramfs kernel happens to round to exactly 0x1500000 and boots, while
the squashfs kernel rounds to 0x1100000 and hangs.

Upstream fixed this for 6.12/6.18 in 9836f7ca132b; kernel 6.6 has no
backport, so carry it here until Parker moves off 24.10.

Fixes: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/issues/23112

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ...-WS-AP3715i-bootwrapper-link-address.patch | 73 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 73 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 patches/openwrt/0021-mpc85xx-fix-WS-AP3715i-bootwrapper-link-address.patch

diff --git a/patches/openwrt/0021-mpc85xx-fix-WS-AP3715i-bootwrapper-link-address.patch b/patches/openwrt/0021-mpc85xx-fix-WS-AP3715i-bootwrapper-link-address.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9200770
--- /dev/null
+++ b/patches/openwrt/0021-mpc85xx-fix-WS-AP3715i-bootwrapper-link-address.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,73 @@
+From 3368b202272bc4413f8f87810ba9f910a0e3e3eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
+Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 17:00:00 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] mpc85xx: fix WS-AP3715i bootwrapper link address
+
+p1010.mk pins KERNEL_ENTRY/KERNEL_LOADADDR to 0x1500000 for the
+Enterasys WS-AP3715i, but the device boots a simpleImage and
+arch/powerpc/boot/wrapper chooses the wrapper's *link* address itself.
+Every other mpc85xx simpleImage device is listed in the case that sets
+link_address='0x1500000'; 109-powerpc-85xx-ws-ap3715i-support.patch adds
+the board and its simpleImage target but never touches boot/wrapper, so
+ws-ap3715i falls through to simpleboot-*, keeps the 0x400000 default and
+gets make_space=y, which rewrites the link address to
+
+  round_size=$(((strip_size + 0xfffff) & 0xfff00000))
+
+i.e. the uncompressed kernel size rounded up to the next MiB. The link
+address therefore tracks the kernel size while the uImage header stays
+constant, and whenever the two disagree U-Boot enters the
+position-dependent wrapper at the wrong address and the board dies
+before the bootwrapper can print anything. On this board the wrapper
+console never registers at all - not even on a successful boot - so the
+failure looks like a dead CPU right after "Uncompressing Kernel Image
+... OK".
+
+That is why it looked like a squashfs-vs-initramfs problem on 24.10:
+the initramfs kernel happened to round to exactly 0x1500000, while the
+squashfs kernel rounds to 0x1100000 and hangs. Measured on real images:
+
+  24.10.3 initramfs   vmlinux.strip 0x14ce094 -> 0x1500000   boots
+  24.10.3 sysupgrade  vmlinux.strip 0x10e8094 -> 0x1100000   hangs
+  25.12.5 initramfs   vmlinux.strip 0x1520894 -> 0x1600000   hangs
+  25.12.5 sysupgrade  vmlinux.strip 0x10f0894 -> 0x1100000   hangs
+
+Verified on hardware: taking the stock 25.12.5 sysupgrade image and
+changing only the uImage load/entry field from 0x1500000 to 0x1100000
+boots Linux 6.12.94 to userspace, and an OpenWrt snapshot build (which
+already carries the fix) boots unmodified.
+
+Add ws-ap3715i to the existing list rather than backporting upstream's
+larger refactor, so no other device's link address changes.
+
+Upstream fixes this in 9836f7ca132b ("mpc85xx: unify wrapper address of
+simple image devices") for 6.12/6.18 only; 24.10 / kernel 6.6 has no
+backport.
+
+Fixes: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/issues/23112
+
+Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
+---
+ ...-85xx-ws-ap3715i-fix-bootwrapper-link-address.patch | 10 ++++++++++
+ 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)
+ create mode 100644 target/linux/mpc85xx/patches-6.6/111-powerpc-85xx-ws-ap3715i-fix-bootwrapper-link-address.patch
+
+diff --git a/target/linux/mpc85xx/patches-6.6/111-powerpc-85xx-ws-ap3715i-fix-bootwrapper-link-address.patch b/target/linux/mpc85xx/patches-6.6/111-powerpc-85xx-ws-ap3715i-fix-bootwrapper-link-address.patch
+new file mode 100644
+index 0000000..663f5d5
+--- /dev/null
++++ b/target/linux/mpc85xx/patches-6.6/111-powerpc-85xx-ws-ap3715i-fix-bootwrapper-link-address.patch
+@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
++--- a/arch/powerpc/boot/wrapper
+++++ b/arch/powerpc/boot/wrapper
++@@ -352,6 +352,7 @@ adder875-redboot)
++ simpleboot-hiveap-330|\
++ simpleboot-tl-wdr4900-v1|\
++ simpleboot-ws-ap3710i|\
+++simpleboot-ws-ap3715i|\
++ simpleboot-ws-ap3825i)
++     platformo="$object/fixed-head.o $object/simpleboot.o"
++     link_address='0x1500000'
+-- 
+2.54.0
